WEBVTT

00:15.473 --> 00:16.641
Hey, Minato.

00:21.354 --> 00:23.398
Koyun, do- do you like her?

00:30.905 --> 00:32.032
I'd see her around.

00:33.199 --> 00:36.411
And she stood out to me, cause she seemed
different from the other girls at our

00:36.494 --> 00:37.328
school.

00:37.871 --> 00:39.205
So her face stuck with me.

00:40.498 --> 00:41.332
And then...

00:43.752 --> 00:44.586
Huh?

00:47.047 --> 00:48.006
She's alone again.

00:49.424 --> 00:52.093
I was always curious about her whenever
I saw her...

00:52.177 --> 00:53.636
Ever since.

00:55.096 --> 00:57.766
I guess you could say I feel sorry
for her.

01:00.018 --> 01:00.852
Minato.

01:02.228 --> 01:04.773
You always do this to people.

01:04.856 --> 01:07.525
You're always pointing out those who
are on their own and feeling sorry for

01:07.609 --> 01:11.279
them.
But that- that's just so arrogant of you.

01:11.988 --> 01:12.906
I'm arrogant?

01:14.365 --> 01:15.408
You really are.

01:16.993 --> 01:19.496
You feel sorry for people without even
knowing them.

01:19.579 --> 01:22.874
Do you realize how they'd feel
to learn you were only nice to them

01:22.957 --> 01:23.792
out of pity?

01:24.501 --> 01:25.752
You have this savior complex.

01:25.835 --> 01:27.337
You want them to rely on you.

01:27.837 --> 01:29.923
So, in the end, it makes you feel needed.

01:30.632 --> 01:33.134
Koyun does not deserve to be one of your
projects!

03:01.598 --> 03:03.933
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

03:07.729 --> 03:11.733
EPISODE 4
IMPENETRABLE

03:12.775 --> 03:16.529
Minato, you shouldn't look at her as just
another sad soul for you to pity.

03:17.405 --> 03:21.117
She's a person, not a charity case so you
can feel good about yourself.

03:22.660 --> 03:24.537
You know, I think you've got a point.

03:25.496 --> 03:26.998
But I don't feel that way now.

03:27.790 --> 03:31.294
When I first saw her, I did feel
bad for her because she always seemed

03:31.377 --> 03:32.378
to be alone.

03:33.421 --> 03:35.048
But that's clearly changed.

03:36.424 --> 03:37.258
Now...

03:39.636 --> 03:41.221
I'm interested for other reasons.

03:41.304 --> 03:42.263
So don't worry.

03:42.347 --> 03:43.348
Huh?

03:43.431 --> 03:46.559
Well, um, I don't think guys like you are
exactly her type.

03:47.060 --> 03:48.186
That's not what I meant.

03:48.269 --> 03:51.481
And even if I did mean it that way,
at least sugarcoat it. Jeez!

03:51.564 --> 03:52.732
Whatever!

03:53.274 --> 03:55.526
Don't try to put the moves on her
or be weird!

03:55.610 --> 03:56.486
Hey, I mean...

03:56.569 --> 03:58.446
No harm in talking to her.

03:59.280 --> 04:01.199
What're you, like her prison warden?

04:02.408 --> 04:04.494
Helicopter parenting is bad for children.

04:06.204 --> 04:07.247
I just don't want...

04:08.081 --> 04:10.625
I just don't want to hurt Koyun anymore.

04:11.292 --> 04:14.003
Don't you mean you don't want her to get
hurt anymore?

04:14.087 --> 04:16.214
Uh... Hold on.

04:16.297 --> 04:19.884
Is Hikawa the girl from the basketball
team?

04:21.344 --> 04:22.178
Ha! I knew it.

04:22.804 --> 04:25.390
Well, now I can see why you're
so protective.

04:25.473 --> 04:26.474
FLUSTERED, FLUSTERED

04:31.062 --> 04:34.857
See? This is why I didn't want Koyun
and Minato getting to know each other!

04:34.941 --> 04:37.735
Wait, why is it okay for Yota but not me?

04:38.319 --> 04:40.989
Because you have these crazy, fine-tuned
instincts.

04:41.072 --> 04:43.074
You're saying Yota isn't perceptive?

04:43.157 --> 04:44.033
Well, no, I...

04:44.117 --> 04:45.243
That's pretty rude, y'know.

04:45.326 --> 04:46.160
I meant...

04:49.580 --> 04:50.498
Oh, wow.

04:50.581 --> 04:51.416
Impressive.

04:51.499 --> 04:53.918
The size of your hand is like a sumo
wrestler's.

04:54.877 --> 04:56.963
- Yo!
- Is that a compliment, or...

04:57.046 --> 04:58.256
You're so lucky.

04:58.339 --> 04:59.173
Am I?

04:59.966 --> 05:03.928
When I played basketball, I always
wanted to palm it like this.

05:04.012 --> 05:04.929
Oops.

05:05.013 --> 05:06.639
But I could never pull it off.

05:06.723 --> 05:08.850
That would be pretty hard on your hands.

05:11.477 --> 05:13.271
Wait, hold on. You were...

05:13.354 --> 05:14.522
You played basketball?

05:15.023 --> 05:16.566
Why didn't you say anything?

05:17.066 --> 05:20.111
Oh, cause I wasn't nearly as committed
to it as you were.

05:20.903 --> 05:22.447
And I quit halfway through.

05:24.824 --> 05:25.658
Wait...

05:33.833 --> 05:36.252
The shame from learning someone was
pitying you...

05:37.545 --> 05:38.379
Is that...

05:39.047 --> 05:40.131
Is that how you felt?

05:40.631 --> 05:42.800
Since I first came up and talked to you?

05:42.884 --> 05:43.926
Uh!

05:44.010 --> 05:45.053
Well, I...

05:45.136 --> 05:47.597
- Flustered, flustered!
- You know, I don't really...

05:48.431 --> 05:49.265
I'm sorry.

05:49.932 --> 05:51.559
That really wasn't my intention.

05:54.854 --> 05:57.273
S CRAM SCHOOL INCREASE YOUR CHANCES FOR
PASSING!

06:00.151 --> 06:03.112
- I first talked to you because you
- RIGHT BEFORE THE EXAM! MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

06:03.196 --> 06:06.491
- looked bored all by yourself.
- HIGHEST ACCEPTANCE RATE IN HISTORY

06:06.574 --> 06:07.408
But...

06:07.492 --> 06:10.244
Once I got to know you, I never saw
you that way again.

06:10.787 --> 06:15.833
Since you and I became friends, and then
Yota joined us, I've had so much fun.

06:17.168 --> 06:19.837
I didn't realize you felt all this doubt
and shame.

06:21.422 --> 06:23.132
I'm sorry for making you feel bad.

06:26.636 --> 06:27.470
Minato.

06:30.390 --> 06:32.517
- Whoa.
- Back it up, buddy. You're too close!

06:32.600 --> 06:35.770
Back it up!
I've had a lot of fun with you too.

06:36.646 --> 06:38.231
And you've helped me out a lot!

06:39.482 --> 06:40.316
Jeez!

06:40.400 --> 06:43.152
So, let's keep being friends, okay?

06:47.490 --> 06:48.324
RUB RUB

06:48.408 --> 06:49.992
Your sweater's gonna get dirty.

06:51.327 --> 06:53.538
It wasn't really all that clean to begin
with.

06:53.621 --> 06:54.455
Yeah. Good idea.

06:55.331 --> 06:56.165
Huh?

06:58.334 --> 07:00.086
I guess maybe...

07:01.087 --> 07:04.340
In the end, what I really wanted
was to feel like I was equal in this

07:04.424 --> 07:07.677
friendship, and not just someone he
felt sorry for.

07:10.221 --> 07:12.807
Ugh, I'm such a baby!

07:15.059 --> 07:15.893
Miki?

07:17.186 --> 07:19.313
Yeah, yeah, hold your horses!

07:20.606 --> 07:23.234
Those two just went to buy drinks, right?

07:23.985 --> 07:25.486
Why is it taking them so long?

07:25.570 --> 07:26.404
SLUMP

07:26.487 --> 07:28.448
- They're growing all the cacao
- FOR COCOA

07:28.531 --> 07:30.324
- beans first?
- From scratch?

07:31.242 --> 07:32.910
- Oh.
- Oh.

07:32.994 --> 07:34.704
Sorry for the wait, we're back!

07:34.787 --> 07:36.122
Look, a new flavor.

07:36.205 --> 07:37.457
DOUBLE EXTRA AZUKI BEAN SOUP—RICH

07:37.540 --> 07:38.749
Double Extra Azuki Bean Soup - Rich.

07:38.833 --> 07:40.835
FULL OF BEAN TEXTURE RICH WITH
AZUKI BEANS' SWEETNESS

07:40.918 --> 07:43.379
- We all have to try!
- She said we have no choice.

07:44.338 --> 07:46.048
- Mm?
- Mm?

07:49.135 --> 07:51.554
Not what I expected, but it should
keep us awake.

07:51.637 --> 07:52.805
That's right!

07:52.889 --> 07:55.475
It should at least help us power through
our exams.

07:56.017 --> 07:58.436
Why does Miki look like she's
been crying?

08:02.732 --> 08:04.984
Should I... maybe ask her?

08:07.278 --> 08:08.112
Miki.

08:09.405 --> 08:13.326
Did something happen with Amamiya
when you guys went to buy drinks?

08:14.035 --> 08:15.244
Huh? Oh, we...

08:15.328 --> 08:17.455
- DON'T GET CLOSE TO KOYUN FOR REASONS LIKE
- I mean, um...

08:17.538 --> 08:18.372
THAT

08:18.456 --> 08:19.290
We just chatted.

08:19.373 --> 08:22.460
He did tell me about the time you
bought a curry drink, though.

08:22.543 --> 08:23.544
Why?

08:24.170 --> 08:27.423
He said that he made you buy it
accidentally, so he paid for all of

08:27.507 --> 08:28.341
our drinks today.

08:28.424 --> 08:30.009
THOUGH HE DIDN'T SAY IT HIMSELF

08:30.092 --> 08:31.385
What? He really didn't need to.

08:31.469 --> 08:34.472
See? He didn't tell you cause he
knew you'd feel bad about it.

08:34.555 --> 08:37.683
- 1, X, 2, SOCIETY, W, HAN DYNASTY, ICE,
- Oh, wait. I'm forgetting what we just

08:37.767 --> 08:38.726
- ROME, H2O
- studied!

08:38.809 --> 08:40.353
I need to review! Where's my notebook?

08:40.436 --> 08:42.313
Ugh, c'mon, come back, come back!

08:43.856 --> 08:47.777
If that's all, it still doesn't
explain what might've made her cry.

08:51.822 --> 08:54.242
Time to finally put all that studying and
cramming behind us.

08:54.325 --> 08:57.119
FIRST PERIOD: ENGLISH COMMUNICATION I
SECOND PERIOD: PUBLIC STUDIES THIRD

08:57.203 --> 08:59.413
PERIOD: BASIC CHEMISTRY, SHR NUMBER OF
STUDENTS: 30

08:59.497 --> 09:00.456
First day of exams.

09:01.457 --> 09:02.416
And begin.

09:07.004 --> 09:07.838
Hm?

09:08.589 --> 09:10.007
It's exactly the same.

09:10.091 --> 09:11.676
Thank you, past exams.

09:13.761 --> 09:16.138
We've been over this problem already with
Yota!

09:24.814 --> 09:26.107
Off to a good start!

09:26.190 --> 09:27.024
Yay!

09:29.485 --> 09:30.987
FIRST PERIOD: LANGUAGE CULTURE 9:00–9:50

09:31.070 --> 09:31.904
SECOND PERIOD: LOGIC AND EXPRESSION AND

09:31.988 --> 09:32.822
I've got this. I've actually got this!

09:32.905 --> 09:34.865
EXPRESSION 10:00–10:50

09:40.538 --> 09:42.790
THIRD PERIOD: GEOGRAPHY 11:00–11:50

09:42.873 --> 09:44.584
- FOURTH PERIOD: BIOLOGY 12:00–12:50
- Alright.

09:44.667 --> 09:45.501
Your time's up.

10:04.395 --> 10:05.479
Notifications?

10:06.188 --> 10:08.774
- NINE MIKI: 9 NOTIFICATIONS
- And quite a few of them.

10:08.858 --> 10:09.942
Koyun.

10:10.026 --> 10:12.236
Let's grab lunch somewhere on
the way home.

10:12.320 --> 10:13.487
Oops, group chat.

10:13.571 --> 10:14.530
Wanna join Yota?

10:14.614 --> 10:16.616
You're not an afterthought, I swear!

10:16.699 --> 10:17.533
Please come.

10:18.075 --> 10:19.660
Sure, I'll come.

10:19.744 --> 10:20.995
Koyun, come on!

10:22.538 --> 10:24.040
Oh, there you are, Koyun.

10:26.876 --> 10:29.462
Looks like you and I are the first ones
to meet up.

10:30.087 --> 10:31.881
Miki's still in the classroom?

10:34.925 --> 10:36.010
What's going on?

10:36.969 --> 10:37.845
What's wrong, Miki?

10:37.928 --> 10:40.097
Oh, Minato. Yota...?

10:40.181 --> 10:41.307
He went downstairs.

10:41.390 --> 10:43.351
Wait, did he leave already?

10:43.434 --> 10:44.644
Need something from him?

10:45.311 --> 10:48.939
It's just Koyun, Yota, and I, we made
lunch plans.

10:51.400 --> 10:53.861
- What gives, Miki?
- Ah! It's freezing!

10:53.944 --> 10:56.614
Are you trying to leave me out of
your good time?

10:56.697 --> 10:58.658
N- N- No that's, uh, not it at all!

10:58.741 --> 11:00.493
BUOONO BUONO!!

11:01.410 --> 11:02.244
Stare.

11:03.704 --> 11:06.248
What?
Five more? I can't tell what's different.

11:06.749 --> 11:07.958
The grapes maybe?

11:08.042 --> 11:09.126
It isn't.

11:09.210 --> 11:10.670
I found a difference.

11:10.753 --> 11:12.213
- BUOONO BUONO!! MENU
- And another one.

11:12.296 --> 11:14.507
- Oh.
- Jeez, you're too fast. Hold up.

11:15.091 --> 11:18.052
If we don't find all of 'em soon,
our food's not gonna come.

11:18.135 --> 11:19.553
Is that really how it works?

11:21.305 --> 11:24.266
They're just acting like regular friends.

11:25.017 --> 11:25.851
I'm glad.

11:27.269 --> 11:30.356
SPACING OUT

11:30.439 --> 11:32.108
Am I reading too much into it?

11:32.191 --> 11:34.026
Have you been here before, Hikawa?

11:34.110 --> 11:34.944
Hm?

11:35.444 --> 11:36.487
Not really.

11:36.570 --> 11:37.405
First time.

11:38.239 --> 11:40.783
I don't normally go anywhere after
school.

11:42.493 --> 11:43.619
Uh. Whoa.

11:45.037 --> 11:47.331
Is that pity I see creeping into
your eyes?

11:47.832 --> 11:48.833
Is it?

11:49.625 --> 11:50.710
That's not it.

11:51.419 --> 11:53.129
- CAFÉ RESTAURANT BUOONO BUONO!!
- Bon appetit!

11:53.212 --> 11:54.338
- Bon appetit!
- Bon appetit!

11:54.422 --> 11:56.340
It was cheap but actually pretty good.

12:00.636 --> 12:01.679
So, Hikawa...

12:02.263 --> 12:03.848
You're not in any clubs, right?

12:04.432 --> 12:05.558
Do you work part-time?

12:06.267 --> 12:07.226
Uh, yeah.

12:07.727 --> 12:10.062
But honestly, I don't work that
many shifts.

12:10.146 --> 12:11.188
Where do you work?

12:11.689 --> 12:13.649
REGULAR CUSTOMERS

12:13.733 --> 12:16.694
A laid-back spot only the elderly in the
neighborhood come to.

12:16.777 --> 12:20.448
- It's just a local restaurant.
- So then what do you do in your free time?

12:20.531 --> 12:22.658
- Give it a rest, would you?
- Good question.

12:22.742 --> 12:23.993
How do I spend my time?

12:25.536 --> 12:26.537
I read books.

12:30.124 --> 12:32.168
What is this? It looks boring.

12:32.877 --> 12:34.086
I watch movies.

12:34.628 --> 12:36.297
Is this even interesting?

12:37.006 --> 12:38.299
And I study ahead.

12:38.799 --> 12:40.092
You're such a nerd.

12:42.303 --> 12:43.429
Nothing, really.

12:44.764 --> 12:46.682
Just space out most of the time.

12:47.892 --> 12:48.726
Oh, really?

12:49.268 --> 12:50.436
That's kind of a shame.

12:50.978 --> 12:51.812
Glare!

12:52.396 --> 12:54.774
Koyun spends her free time hanging out
with me!

12:54.857 --> 12:55.983
Does she really?

13:01.614 --> 13:03.032
Are you paying separately?

13:03.115 --> 13:03.991
Yes.

13:04.492 --> 13:06.410
- Hey. Minato, what are you doing?
- Mm?

13:06.994 --> 13:08.329
What's with the interrogation?

13:08.412 --> 13:09.538
I told you, didn't I?

13:10.122 --> 13:11.665
Well, I figured...

13:12.708 --> 13:15.377
If we were the only ones involved in
the conversation, she'd be bored.

13:15.461 --> 13:17.129
- SLICK, SLICK
- Oh!

13:17.213 --> 13:18.881
- You have a point!
- Right?

13:22.802 --> 13:26.138
All of these questions are kind of
exhausting.

13:29.016 --> 13:31.435
- Whew, man, I am crazy full.
- The people and environment are so

13:31.519 --> 13:32.728
different from back then.

13:32.812 --> 13:34.188
I'm going to burst.

13:34.855 --> 13:37.650
I'm still not very good at talking about
myself.

13:39.276 --> 13:40.861
I don't hate him or anything.

13:41.445 --> 13:44.448
But I'm scared of people finding out
who I am on the inside.

13:45.199 --> 13:47.076
I'm trying to avoid rejection.

13:47.785 --> 13:50.746
To avoid hating myself more than I
already do.

13:52.206 --> 13:55.501
That's why I keep my distance when
people try to get close to me.

13:55.584 --> 13:57.044
God, you're such a weirdo.

13:57.127 --> 13:57.962
You know that?

14:00.130 --> 14:01.465
What is normal anyway?

14:05.469 --> 14:06.470
SECOND TRIMESTER FINAL EXAMS DAY 3

14:06.554 --> 14:07.388
FIRST PERIOD: MODERN JAPANESE 09:00–09:50

14:07.471 --> 14:08.305
Good job! We nailed those exams!

14:08.389 --> 14:10.641
SECOND PERIOD: BASIC BIOLOGY 10:00–10:50

14:10.724 --> 14:11.767
EXAM AFTER-PARTY CLASS 1-5

14:11.851 --> 14:12.685
- Yay!
- Yay!

14:12.768 --> 14:15.104
- Yay!
- It looks delicious. Do you wanna try it?

14:15.187 --> 14:16.522
Sure, I'll have a bite.

14:16.605 --> 14:17.523
Ahh.

14:18.023 --> 14:20.776
Azumi is absolutely glowing today.

14:25.197 --> 14:26.657
I'm sick to my stomach.

14:27.533 --> 14:30.077
I somehow managed to get through
the exams, but...

14:30.160 --> 14:32.746
My stomach feels so queasy.

14:33.747 --> 14:34.957
SCHOOL NURSE'S OFFICE

14:35.457 --> 14:36.959
- Noriko.
- Huh?

14:37.459 --> 14:38.502
Help.

14:38.586 --> 14:40.546
Are you seriously back here already?

14:41.046 --> 14:43.799
I keep telling you this isn't the place
to get warm.

14:43.883 --> 14:45.926
I'm actually sick today, I swear.

14:47.011 --> 14:47.845
Oh.

14:53.309 --> 14:54.268
It's my stomach.

14:55.352 --> 14:56.896
Oh no. You stressed?

14:56.979 --> 14:58.981
Or did you eat something you shouldn't
have?

14:59.064 --> 15:01.233
I haven't eaten anything today.

15:01.775 --> 15:04.069
Oh, I had three cups of coffee, though.

15:05.237 --> 15:06.280
That'll do it.

15:06.363 --> 15:08.282
Okay, you can sleep it off here.

15:08.991 --> 15:11.535
I can't get comfortable laying in
my uniform.

15:11.619 --> 15:13.287
Alright, don't push it, kid.

15:18.959 --> 15:21.545
Did you go to junior high with anyone
here at Meiten?

15:21.629 --> 15:23.422
I did actually. He was a nerd.

15:24.340 --> 15:26.759
Well, yeah, you have to be smart to
get in here.

15:28.260 --> 15:29.386
What about you, Igarashi?

15:29.470 --> 15:30.304
You know anyone?

15:30.888 --> 15:31.722
Ah?

15:32.890 --> 15:34.308
I have no idea.

15:34.391 --> 15:36.977
No one I know would get in here.

15:38.145 --> 15:40.105
We have some snacks left, I think.

15:40.773 --> 15:41.815
Did we buy too much?

15:41.899 --> 15:43.567
- Yeah, we might have.
- Mm-hm.

15:43.651 --> 15:44.985
Aren't those guys from West High?

15:45.069 --> 15:45.986
Mm.

15:46.070 --> 15:46.904
Huh?

15:48.405 --> 15:49.323
Igarashi?

15:51.075 --> 15:53.243
- What the... What?
- What?

16:00.501 --> 16:03.545
Head on home.
I gotta catch up with someone.

16:04.046 --> 16:05.130
Okay, have fun.

16:06.048 --> 16:06.882
Bye, Miki.

16:07.967 --> 16:08.842
Why are you here?

16:11.428 --> 16:12.262
Azumi.

16:13.222 --> 16:14.056
You...

16:14.556 --> 16:15.432
I what?

16:16.558 --> 16:18.769
You just look so different than you
used to.

16:19.436 --> 16:20.521
Where'd "gorilla" go?

16:21.689 --> 16:23.148
Shut up! Do not call me that!

16:24.024 --> 16:24.858
Mm.

16:27.778 --> 16:28.612
Hm?

16:28.696 --> 16:30.364
Why're you at this school?

16:30.447 --> 16:31.365
Huh?

16:31.448 --> 16:32.908
I'm here for club activities.

16:33.450 --> 16:35.619
We have a joint soccer practice.

16:37.162 --> 16:39.790
By the way, I didn't know you went to
Meiten.

16:40.416 --> 16:44.044
I bet you're probably the only one
who commutes this far every day, huh?

16:44.586 --> 16:45.421
Why bother?

16:46.338 --> 16:48.841
I guess he doesn't know Koyun goes here
too.

16:49.758 --> 16:50.592
Hm?

16:51.176 --> 16:52.720
Hey! Igarashi!

16:52.803 --> 16:53.971
What's the hold up?

16:54.471 --> 16:55.431
Oh.

16:56.181 --> 16:57.057
Oh, sorry.

16:57.599 --> 16:58.642
See ya later.

17:02.312 --> 17:03.397
Who was that girl?

17:03.480 --> 17:04.440
She's so cute.

17:04.523 --> 17:06.108
Dude, get your eyes checked.

17:06.191 --> 17:07.234
Huh?

17:08.110 --> 17:08.944
Koyun.

17:09.028 --> 17:11.697
Please tell me you've already gone
home from school.

17:17.202 --> 17:19.747
So dark. Wait. What time is it?

17:20.914 --> 17:23.333
Oh, it's just because the curtains were
closed.

17:23.417 --> 17:24.918
Thanks, Noriko.

17:26.045 --> 17:29.631
It's still pretty bright outside, so
at least it hasn't been that long.

17:35.888 --> 17:36.722
Igarashi!

17:38.098 --> 17:39.224
Right, that was today!

17:39.975 --> 17:42.936
Well, he's visiting our school soon,
but you don't know each other, so never

17:43.020 --> 17:44.897
- mind.
- When?

17:44.980 --> 17:47.066
For a scrimmage on the last day of exams.

17:48.525 --> 17:49.777
He told me about it, but...

17:50.944 --> 17:51.987
Oh, by the way...

17:52.696 --> 17:54.490
Earlier, I ran into Azumi.

17:54.990 --> 17:56.825
Are you two classmates?

17:56.909 --> 17:58.327
Oh. Miki?

17:58.410 --> 17:59.995
Not classmates, but friends.

18:01.205 --> 18:03.082
So, is she causing trouble here too?

18:03.165 --> 18:04.458
She broken any windows?

18:06.085 --> 18:07.044
Nah, she's great.

18:07.544 --> 18:10.464
Earlier, I ran into Azumi. Are you two
classmates?

18:10.547 --> 18:12.007
They're talking about Miki.

18:12.091 --> 18:13.759
- Oh, Miki?
- Why?

18:13.842 --> 18:15.177
Not classmates, but friends

18:15.260 --> 18:16.512
Agh, I can't hear them very well.

18:16.595 --> 18:17.930
...Causing trouble here too?

18:19.223 --> 18:20.933
Hikawa. What are you doing?

18:22.226 --> 18:23.685
Um, I was just...

18:24.228 --> 18:25.687
Are you feeling any better?

18:25.771 --> 18:26.605
Yeah, I'm fine.

18:27.106 --> 18:29.441
- Can you go home?
- Yes.

18:32.820 --> 18:34.822
I'm gonna book it so he won't notice me.

18:38.242 --> 18:41.787
I couldn't hear everything, but they were
definitely talking about Miki.

18:41.870 --> 18:44.039
They're not gonna talk about me,
are they?

18:47.584 --> 18:51.505
I wonder if Amamiya will bring me up.

18:52.631 --> 18:53.799
You know Igarashi?

18:54.508 --> 18:57.469
Where do you work?
Whadda you do in your spare time?

18:57.553 --> 18:58.929
SO CURIOUS ABOUT OTHER PEOPLE

18:59.012 --> 18:59.847
I bet he will.

19:02.224 --> 19:03.058
I'd hate that.

19:04.685 --> 19:07.020
I don't want people having any
interest in me.

19:12.860 --> 19:16.113
I don't want anyone to know my true self.

19:17.990 --> 19:18.824
Oh.

19:18.907 --> 19:22.202
By the way, Igarashi, do you remember
Hikawa?

19:25.497 --> 19:26.331
Huh?

19:36.884 --> 19:37.926
Oh, Hikawa!

19:40.304 --> 19:41.763
Hey there! Good morning!

19:41.847 --> 19:42.890
Eh?

19:42.973 --> 19:45.142
Why does he look all warm like that?

19:48.770 --> 19:50.606
Oh! We just finished morning practice.

19:50.689 --> 19:52.649
- Amamiya, did you run here, or something?
- I'm steaming from the cold.

19:52.733 --> 19:54.735
Morning practice. Boy, I remember those.

19:56.862 --> 20:00.032
Oh.
By the way, Igarashi was here yesterday.

20:02.326 --> 20:03.160
Although...

20:03.827 --> 20:05.370
You don't really care, do you?

20:06.079 --> 20:09.041
Seems like you weren't close friends
with him, or anything.

20:10.959 --> 20:11.793
Huh?

20:11.877 --> 20:13.212
Where did that come from?

20:14.087 --> 20:17.174
Tell me, was Igarashi super popular
back in junior high?

20:18.300 --> 20:20.385
Well, I mean, I guess so.

20:21.428 --> 20:24.306
He was always the center of attention.

20:24.389 --> 20:27.017
- With people constantly around him.
- I knew it.

20:27.517 --> 20:29.019
Figured he was like that.

20:30.020 --> 20:33.941
He's the kind of person who just butts
his nose into other people's business...

20:34.024 --> 20:35.192
Without even asking.

20:36.151 --> 20:37.945
Oh. I'm sorry.

20:38.445 --> 20:40.697
Let's stop talking about junior high.

20:44.493 --> 20:45.327
Hey, don't worry.

20:45.410 --> 20:47.621
You'll make all new memories in
high school.

20:48.372 --> 20:51.166
There's a lot of events, and fun stuff
coming up.

20:53.085 --> 20:55.879
There's the dance, and field day too.
Oh, and don't forget soccer season.

20:55.963 --> 20:57.714
Speaking of which, any chance you
might come to some of our games?

20:57.798 --> 21:00.217
I've never talked to Amamiya about my
memories from junior high school, so...

21:00.300 --> 21:01.885
Why'd he suddenly mention them?

21:02.803 --> 21:03.929
Did he hear something?

21:04.471 --> 21:05.555
From Igarashi?

21:06.556 --> 21:08.308
What did he tell him?

21:09.268 --> 21:11.186
Koyuki. Oh my gosh, no way!

21:11.270 --> 21:12.771
You're really dating Igarashi?

21:13.272 --> 21:14.189
So...

21:14.273 --> 21:15.607
How far have you two gone?

21:17.276 --> 21:18.110
It's funny.

21:18.193 --> 21:19.653
She only seems to be nice to guys,
am I right?

21:19.736 --> 21:21.363
I know, right? What a "pick-me."

21:22.364 --> 21:23.740
- Did you know?
- Igarashi is...

21:23.824 --> 21:24.825
I heard Koyuki's family is...

21:24.908 --> 21:26.618
- No way.
- You're kidding!

21:27.953 --> 21:28.787
What? Seriously?

21:28.870 --> 21:31.498
- Why does everyone love rumors and
- So that rumor was true.

21:31.581 --> 21:34.459
- Gossip so much?
- Why can't they just leave me alone?

21:34.543 --> 21:36.003
Hey, Koyuki.

21:37.629 --> 21:40.299
Do you get some sick pleasure in
meddling in my life?

21:40.799 --> 21:42.718
What's really going on with you two?

21:43.593 --> 21:45.304
You don't care if it's true or not...

21:45.387 --> 21:47.597
Just as long as it's entertaining, right?

21:52.811 --> 21:53.770
Well, I'm done.

21:56.982 --> 21:58.150
Mind your own business.

21:59.693 --> 22:01.361
- I don't get it.
- Uh?

22:02.612 --> 22:03.447
WARM, WARM

22:03.530 --> 22:05.115
Ah, the cold air feels so good.

22:07.117 --> 22:07.951
Huh?

22:08.035 --> 22:10.370
- Koyu-
- Why do you have to be such a busybody?

22:15.000 --> 22:16.084
I don't understand.

22:19.588 --> 22:20.672
It makes me sick.
